With all you people discussing whether rings of conflict are too powerful
and should, there's one more item that IMHO should be added to the list
of potentially too powerful items: the Helms of Opposite Alignment.
I've just found a very nice abuse (?) for the HoOA and I tested it yesterday
and it seemed to work: (SPOILER)


In the endgame, the main challenge is to find the correct altar. 
With a HoOA alignment, you can sacrifice the Amulet on the "wrong" altar
and ascend. A neutral character is powerful indeed: he can pick any altar
he wants to. HoOA makes ascending MUCH easier for neutral characters...
(add that to other nice things like getting out of Gehennom as chaotic or
not getting attacked as easily by angels as lawful...)

I don't know about the rest of you, but *I* think this takes quite a lot
away from the challenge of the Astral Plane. 
Maybe HoOA should always be cursed and impossible to uncurse?

